   "text": {
    "L1": "Many communities protect nature through knowledge passed down over time.",
    "L2": "MYTH: Traditional practices have nothing to teach science.",
    "L3": "That is not true. Neem leaves help keep insects away, and stored rainwater helps in dry months.",
    "L4": "A sacred grove is a forest patch people do not cut. Plants, animals and water sources stay safer there.",
    "L5": "Roots hold soil, and rainwater can soak into the ground and slowly feed a spring.",
    "L6": "A standing tree gives more than wood: it gives shade, fruit, animal homes and soil protection.",
    "L7": "People can make a difference. Bishnoi people protected khejri trees, and Chipko people hugged trees to stop cutting.",
    "L8": "This care continues from Khejarli, to Chipko, to villages protecting sacred groves today. Put these events in order."
   },
